-- KEEP users.refresh_token (do not drop it). Refresh tokens issued before this deploy are
-- still checked against it once, turned into an auth_sessions row, and the column is then
-- set to NULL. It can be dropped in a later migration, 7+ days after this one ships.
--
-- Emails: register/login trim + lower-case them and the repo matches lower(email), so
-- existing mixed-case rows keep working without a data fix. Login tries the password
-- against each case-only duplicate account (up to 5).
--
-- OPTIONAL follow-up (manager's call, not needed for correctness). Only run it after
-- checking that no two accounts differ by case alone, otherwise the UPDATE/INDEX fails:
--
--   -- SELECT lower(email), count(*) FROM users GROUP BY 1 HAVING count(*) > 1;
--   -- UPDATE users SET email = lower(email) WHERE email <> lower(email);
--   -- CREATE UNIQUE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS users_email_lower_idx ON users (lower(email));
